  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "2002 (Sep. - Oct.): A Two-leg Survey Leg 2 Data of Waters Between Kodiak and Seward, AK - R/V Miller Freeman (Cruise ID: MF2002-11)",
  "description": "The Alaska Fisheries Science Center and Pacific Marine Environmental Laboratory FOCI program conducted a mooring survey in the waters between Kodiak and Seward, Alaska. Data collected include subsurface and surface water temperature and water salinity, chlorophyll, and nutrients. Cruise ID: MF2002-07 (4 - 9 Oct. 2002) Survey vessels: R/V Miller Freeman For preliminary survey results see http://www.pmel.noaa.gov/foci/operations/instructions/2002/MF02-11/MF02-11_L2_report.htm\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To support research into the physical, chemical, and biological mechanisms acting in the coastal Gulf of Alaska. To make a CTD/Chlorophyll/Nutrient survey of Portlock Bank and northern portion of Albatross Bank and Chiniak Trough.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23568146",
